n the ancient past, Oracles were thought to be the instruments through which the gods spoke words of
wisdom, advice, and prophecy. Their words could elucidate or mystify. In this game, the dice and
random tables below stand in for an Oracle. When combined with the imagination of the Referee, a few
short words can be the springboard to fill in a great deal of detail. Sometimes the words may not be
immediately clear, but with time, you might find, the dice are always proven to be right.
The Referee should familiarize himself with the tables so that when a question arises, he can quickly
decide which table to use and get on with preparing or running the game.
Designer Note: These tables were populated using words found in CHAINMAIL 3rd edition.
Anthropic's Claude Artificial Intelligence program was used to parse the text and output the lists. These
tables were the entire leaping off point for writing The Primeval RPG. I wanted to prove that there is
no need for a fancy set of supplements, that the wargame from which the entire fantasy role playing
hobby arose is quite capable of giving a Referee the tools to launch an entire campaign and keep it
going. Many solo players and Referees use a variety of modern books and tools. But like the DNA
contained in a single cell, the wargame is a fertile seed from which to plant, and reap, fields of gold.

